WEBVTT

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:08.040
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.920
Moonlit Guns for Hire

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.380
I'm tellin' ya...

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:20.540
I woulda sworn I'd get myself
a few more tags, but no, nothing!

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.250
Talk about not living up to the hype!

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.420
Gimme a break, Adolfo.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:24.960
Pass.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.380
You fly about as steady as 
a windsock on a latrine.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.710
Pass-What's that even mean?

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:30.420
Pass.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.420
I'm just saying you always wind up
right where I'm trying to avoid.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:31.750
I got nothing.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.790
Swinging 'round aimlessly this way and that.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:38.050
Really, Miguel?

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.500
What's our own ammo-wasting
champion got to laugh about?

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.970
Don't throw a fit now, Adolfo.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:42.540
Bam!

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:43.880
Not so fast.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:50.290
I'm out.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:51.670
Again?!

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.630
This is ridiculous.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.460
Guess we don't stand a chance
against the hand of God himself, eh?

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.830
God had no part in this.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.750
You bet he didn't!
God ain't never helped anyone anywhere!

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:04.710
Both of you be damned.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.170
Ririko, my dear!

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:08.750
I've gotta be the most pitiful chap
in the whole Nazarin Air Squad.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.420
Why doncha come cheer me up?

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.330
That's not on our menu.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.040
Oh, that's cold.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.340
But that's what I love about ya!

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.000
Give it a rest, Adolfo.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.100
If there ain't a single gal in this world
who'd gimme the time of day...

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.540
How do I know I'm not in hell already?

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.580
Sure they might not be friendly,
but we've still got plenty of gals, right?

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:26.710
Where, exactly?

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.580
Here are your pancakes, 
just the way you like them.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:29.540
Hooray!

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.430
Reona, so as I was saying,

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:49.910
I'd like to take two days off after 
this job, but what do you say?

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:51.750
What's this for now, Emma? A date?

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.960
Not at all. I simply need 
to attend to the orchard.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.970
Ah, those Yoshino cherry trees?

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:01.040
The very ones. I can't have them dying off now
that they've been left to me.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.000
The Madame's the one who calls the shots,
but I don't see two days being an issue.

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:06.420
I'll be going to the hospital.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:07.380
Say hi to Allen for me.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:07.960
Right.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.000
Ririko, whip me up some more!

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.670
What are you planning to do, Reona?

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:13.830
The same as always.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.960
You should come out drinking with me.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.250
I'll think about it.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.750
That's basically the same as saying no.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:20.830
You're no fun.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:21.500
Here you are.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.130
Ririko, you're the quickest cook around!

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:27.290
Kylie, you certainly do have
an appetite for pancakes, don't you?

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:29.750
I mean, it has been a whole 
18 hours since my last plate.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:30.960
I fail to see your point.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.670
They're so light and fluffy, with 
just that hint of sweetness.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:36.630
The perfect match to some salted meat
and just the right size, too!

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.540
Plus there's that ultra-lite whipped cream on the side
to give it a boost when it needs it.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.170
Not that they aren't delish as-is!

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:44.580
They taste like something 
you could only dream of!

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.380
Yet the 850 calories on that plate
are anything but a dream.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.080
Well, how are you supposed to enjoy pancakes
if you worry about the calories?

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.420
Who can't handle a scary 
little thrill like this?

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:54.750
Oh, to be young again.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.630
I doubt we could keep up with her.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.790
Johnny's place here has got
the best pancakes around!

00:02:58.790 --> 00:02:59.670
Well, well.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.000
Pardon me!

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.130
The name's Adolfo.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:04.670
We're both off shift in 
another seven hours, yeah?

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:06.460
Sure it's still a bit early, 
but whaddya say we celebrate?

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:10.290
Seven hours is plenty enough time
to find some love in the air, eh?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:11.960
Unfortunately...

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.380
Cursed be any who dare 
disrespect a good pancake!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.130
What?

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:19.710
Oh, sorry. I'm only interested in
these two over here, ya see.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:20.920
Well, that's a shame.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.730
Because Reona here doesn't 
waste her time with men

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:24.090
who couldn't even hold their own against her.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:27.640
Oh yeah? Well, let me introduce myself, then!

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.250
I'm Adolfo Yamada of the Nazarin Air Squad.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.880
I've been at this for five 
years and three months now.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.560
And I've got 11 and 5/7th stars to my name!

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.790
When it comes to lightning fast first strikes
and always being one step ahead, I'm a pro!

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:38.500
Whaddya say? Impressive, yeah?

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.960
Kate, what the heck is 5/7th of a star?

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.500
A number he is still aspiring for.
That is, one he has still yet to earn.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:44.330
Oh!

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.540
But only eleven, huh?

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.460
What?!

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:47.540
Whaddya mean "only" eleven?

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:50.250
Oh well, I mean that's still pretty good
if you're flying a Shiden.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:51.960
"For a Shiden?!"

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.750
Let me tell you a little something about
the gunpods on those wings there-

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:55.420
YIKES!

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.670
Ladies, sorry about our boy Adolfo here.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.050
Quit acting so immature 
around a bunch of kids.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.460
Many thanks for your kindness.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.420
Your friend here certainly seems
quite lively and ambitious.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:07.210
Why would you say that?

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:10.560
Kate, this is what some would 
call "lip service," you see.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:13.000
So you mean, you're lying, then?

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.290
I'd prefer it if you'd 
say I was acting wisely.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.810
Do you really need to go that far, though?

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:18.330
If you hope to get along.

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:19.250
No, thanks!

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.670
With a guy that's acting all tough over
just eleven measly stars? No way!

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:25.630
He ruins the mood, talks himself up,
and gets a big nope from me!

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:27.160
You wanna say that to my face?!

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.430
Well now girly! If you're gonna 
run your mouth off like that,

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:32.300
I take it you got the skills to back it up?

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.170
Yup. Let's see...

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:37.170
I think I'm at 43 now. And that's without
any unofficial, unconfirmed tags.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.790
Forty three?!

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.290
No way! That's impossible!

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:41.080
Unbelievable!

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.000
Believe it.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.300
All of them together have 
tallied up over 200, you know.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:59.070
Why do none of my good hunches

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:01.910
ever come to fruition but the 
bad ones never seem to fail to?

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:07.420
Hey! Howdy! Your dependable First Officer
of the Hagoromo, Saneatsu here!

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:11.000
This alarm is an automatic alert set off
by readings on our radar.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.330
Radar shows movement bearing 340 degrees,
on our two o'clock.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:17.060
We're picking up no large 
aircraft in that direction,

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:19.010
but we have unidentified 
bogey moving in fast.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:20.000
Altitude is 600 khrill.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.130
Cloud base sits at 450 khrill.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.830
Winds are blowing in from 280 degrees.

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:25.460
Wind speed is 4.5 khrill.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:29.670
We are currently positioned at A-E
145 degrees and 54 minutes.

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:31.790
M-B 30 degrees and 17 minutes.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:32.830
What are our fuel reserves?

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:34.380
4,102 bottles.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:37.850
We can maintain course at current speeds
for 695 more kilometers.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:40.000
Which means we have no 
chance of evading them.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.170
What's the speed on those bogeys?

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:43.210
Bogeys moving in at 165 kilometers per hour.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.880
Altitudes like that must mean 
they're flying zeroes, then?

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.540
I take it that means we're 
dealing with air pirates?

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:49.630
Really? Do we have no escape routes?

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:52.210
Tell me Maria, can you 
resist buying new shoes?

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:52.920
Not a chance.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.330
Same goes for me and bags.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:55.540
That's how big of a chance we have here.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.330
Things are looking grim, then.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:58.460
First Officer.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.290
Requesting permission to launch fighters.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:02.250
We're really doing this?

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.630
We're running out of time.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:05.920
So be it!

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:09.790
Permission to launch all fighters!

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:11.130
Oh, and uh...

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.600
All crew to their battle positions!

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.830
Anyone who can't keep up is gonna get
an inertia handle cranked right up their butts!

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:21.630
Roger!

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.790
I thought we'd at least 
get off this time around.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.000
Well, aren't you nauseatingly naïve?

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:58.080
All right, all right! Time 
to tag me a few more stars!

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:58.810
Sure you got it in ya?

00:06:58.810 --> 00:06:59.580
I do!

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:01.350
Fernando, say a prayer for us.

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:04.040
My days of praying are long behind me.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.040
Please.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.460
Hey, check out our little gal's plane.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:21.580
She plays it up with talk of 40 tags,
200 even, but she flies a Hayabusa?

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.580
All girls wanna do is show off.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:24.710
Focus, leave them be.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:25.460
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.000
Attention all crew! Commencing braking!

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:32.830
Nazarin Air Squad, clear for takeoff!

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.080
The Nazarin are good to go already?

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.790
That's what I like about these freelancers!

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.000
First officer, that's the Madame on the line.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:45.710
I'm aware.

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:46.920
Aren't you going to pick up?

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:47.750
'Course I am.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.630
Hey there, Loulou!
Our vessel's got no problems to report!

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:53.920
Well, of course not.

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:56.380
Today's cargo is of particular importance.

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.080
You are aware of this, yes?

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:58.670
Yes, ma'am!

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:02.210
Let my lovely little birdies know
there's a bonus to be had today.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:04.580
For each and every plane they shoot down.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:05.960
For me, too?!

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.920
Lose even a single drop of 
that cargo and you're done.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.920
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:16.130
FUEL

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.560
IGNITION

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:21.310
FUEL PRESSURE

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:24.670
Get her started!

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:31.290
Fire 'er up!

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.030
IGNITION

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:42.830
OIL PRESSURE

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:43.580
RPM

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:00.810
IGNITION

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:09.420
ON
OFF

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:09.920
OFF

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:10.360
ON
OFF

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:32.420
All right. Same as always, two to a team-

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:34.250
No wait, today we're in two 
teams of two and three.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.880
I finally feel awake.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:39.080
Zara, don't you go falling 
asleep on me out here.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:41.710
I'll be fine. I could pilot 
this thing in my sleep.

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:43.210
Don't push your luck.

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:46.040
That's what got Chika in trouble.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:46.920
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:48.380
Kate, Emma, Kylie.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:49.460
The rear's all yours.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.210
As you wish.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:50.870
Roger that.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:52.130
Bogeys sighted, two o'clock.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.290
Oh, this'll be fun!

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:55.630
Fly high, KOTOBUKI Flight Corps!

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:56.380
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:18.420
Think you're good, eh?

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:20.000
Wobbling and fluttering around?

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:20.920
Gotcha!

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.160
Damn! Where'd they go?!

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:36.380
I can't shake 'em!

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:43.920
Rodriguez!

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:44.880
Adolfo, behind you!

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:52.960
Nazarin Squad, three birds down.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:56.330
What?! Didn't these guys say
they were the best of the best?

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:04.330
Did I lose 'em? Did they just give up?!

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:23.220
Something's up. These aren't the regular
sort of pirates we're used to!

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:28.850
Got 'em!

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.170
The Hagoromo's in trouble!

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:03.080
Air pirates, closing in.

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:06.210
Gimme a break! You shoot us down and
there'll be no cargo left for you, you hear me?!

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.290
These horrid pirates!

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.540
Emma sure is something.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.420
Permission to fire granted! Requested even!

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.130
Is that one of ours? One of theirs?!

00:16:58.130 --> 00:16:58.670
It's an enemy craft.

00:16:58.670 --> 00:16:59.330
We aren't going to make it!

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:05.040
Woohoo!

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.040
Kylie, nice work!

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.040
Enemy in retreat. No need for pursuit.

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:10.460
All birds return to nest.

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:28.630
Uh-oh.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.920
Oh no! You're definitely going down!

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:55.970
All right!

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:23.170
What? Huh?!

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:26.390
What? Why? How?!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.130
Not this! Not again!

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:50.710
Urgh, that's so annoying!

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:00.040
The captain's taken flight!

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:01.260
Kylie's home to roost!

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:36.500
You doofus!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.880
How many times do I need to 
tell you to cut that out?!

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:38.500
I just...

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:39.250
I don't want your excuses!

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:45.460
I bet the first officer plans to pay out
bonuses for their families.

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:47.210
I can see where he's coming from.

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:49.850
What, are you telling 
me you like that whiner?

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:54.080
No, I just mean it must be tough to be
the family of a fighter pilot.

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:54.790
Oh.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:57.210
So cocky and full of themselves.

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:59.580
Always looking for another thrill.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:02.420
Reckless and quick to disappear.

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:04.580
Nothing but morons.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:06.000
Where have Reona and the girls gone?

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.580
Couldn't say. They all headed for town
as soon as we landed.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.420
And here I was ready to dish out bonuses.

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:12.920
I'll take it in their stead!

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:14.080
Are you really that dumb?

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.080
I might just be.

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:23.170
Long ago, the world opened right up,
and lots of things rained down on us.

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:25.830
Some good things. Some bad things.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:28.460
Some lovely things. Some tarnished things.

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:30.330
There was all sorts of stuff.

00:21:30.710 --> 00:21:34.250
But since then, things have closed up again.

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:38.040
And now, while we slowly lose
many of the things we have...

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:40.960
We still live on.

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:50.420
Okay! I'll be back!

00:22:14.500 --> 00:22:17.670
Flying through the mesh of clouds

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:21.210
Our dancing wings wrap up in the wind

00:22:21.210 --> 00:22:24.670
Stars fall right before our eyes

00:22:30.670 --> 00:22:33.960
The blue of all blues that drew us in

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:37.040
We kicked up off the blurring ground

00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:42.250
Let me hear the sound of the sky you know

00:22:44.830 --> 00:22:51.580
Take flight make gravity your ally

00:22:51.710 --> 00:22:57.960
One more time, however many 
times, laughing all along

00:22:57.960 --> 00:23:05.000
We would never look back when we fly

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:10.210
An everlasting dream we 
live in pursuit of tomorrow

00:23:10.330 --> 00:23:13.710
Amid rising despair I locked away my love

00:23:13.710 --> 00:23:16.040
I hate my weak self

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:22.000
Here and now passes by as 
we head towards the future

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:27.380
Preview

00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:37.420
Next time on The Magnificent KOTOBUKI,
"The Wandering Six"!

00:23:38.130 --> 00:23:40.880
The Wandering Six
